    "text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is released from the top of a rough incline having&nbsp;<math><mrow><mi>μ</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mtext>.</mtext> </mrow></math>&nbsp;The initial speed of the block is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The inclined plane has unknown length and has a spring of spring constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> connected at the base as in the figure. Find the maximum compression of spring. (answer in meter).<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/260421_ques.JPG\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 123px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
